                  "basis": "assumed",
                  "rationale": "Nobody measured it, and only Whitted put a figure on the flame at all, its length. What both men describe is a jet of orange and red seen against a moonless night from a few hundred metres, bright enough that they took it at first for the exhaust of a jet fighter: 120 000 cd/m² is the order of a rocket motor's plume and a tenth of the Socorro flame's assumed brightness, which was chosen against daylight and would be absurd here. What makes it right or wrong is the eye, not the account: the recording states a luminance so that the scene's own photometry decides how it reads at 02:45, and a better figure replaces this one without anything else changing."
