          "basis": "derived",
          "rationale": "Thirty metres long is the account's own figure. The distance is not: the two men never agreed on it, one under a thousand feet and the other several times that, and McDonald does not say which said which. Both are DERIVED here from the drawing itself, and nothing is derived from the length, which the drawing foreshortens. What it does not foreshorten is the THICKNESS: a body of revolution is its own diameter across the short way from any angle, so the 3.17 m the recording makes of the box's height fixes the range at every instant, 706 m as it comes on and 183 m at its nearest. That the nearest lands on the official report's own framing is not a confirmation: the drawing was laid out to it. The box's WIDTH then says how far round it had turned, 20° off end-on at the first instant and broadside by the last, and the heading that follows from that comes out at 184° on average and never more than fifteen degrees from it: Chiles's boxes, which say nothing about a course, are those of a thing holding one straight course while the aeroplane crossed it. Where it points UP is nowhere: through the pull-up it climbs without raising its nose, because his boxes stay as thin there as anywhere, and a thirty-metre body pitched thirty degrees is five times deeper on the glass than one flying level. Tilting it would manufacture a disagreement he never stated."
